{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla","id":1549587,"title":"Running the Free States - 6 - Petrodon and the Camarilla","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-26T23:44:38-07:00","id":1549587,"title":"Running the Free States - 6 - Petrodon and the Camarilla","content":"The intention of the Camarilla towards the Free States circa the time of the LABN sourcebook can be termed hostile, but not confrontational.<br /> <br /> The princes of the west and midwest are aggressive because they are on the frontlines of anarch attempts to \u201cliberate\u201d more domains. The princes farther east see the Fee States more as a safety valve as their own malcontents are likely to leave for them, rather than continue to agitate at home. (Presumably this is also impacted by the much greater danger of the Sabbat there as well.) These different perspectives have divided opinion inside the Camarilla as to what to do with them.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t until 1984 that the Inner Circle tasked Justicar Petrodon to begin covert operations against the Free State, some forty years after it existed. Then it seems he is waiting to see w hat the Inner Circle will decide in its 1997 meeting before escalting things. (These are the years mentioned in LABN, other sourcebooks seem to indicate the Inner Circle meets in 85 and 98.) So Petrodon is not in full out war against the anarchs. He\u2019s just preparing for the night when that may happen.<br /> <br /> At this time, the main efforts of the Camarilla seem to be interdiction, blockade, and intelligence gathering. Except when dealing with travel to and from the Free States, it is Petrodon\u2019s intelligence agents in LA (and possibly San Francisco should the PCs visit the Vampire Club or SF in general) that will have the most direct impact to an LA chronicle.<br /> <br /> =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council\">Part 1 - the Anarch Council</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine\">Part 2 - Germaine</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance\">Part 3 - Governance</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs\">Part 4 - Canon Characters &amp; Gangs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites\">Part 5 - Setites</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club\">Part 7 - San Francisco</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat\">Part 8 - Sabbat</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements\">Part 9 - Crossovers</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff\">Part 10 - Oddballs</a>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 02-02-2026, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-26T23:45:42-07:00","id":1549588,"title":"","content":"He\u2019s placed several Archons in San Francisco, seemingly to make sure that domain does not fall.<br /> <br /> The Princes of Tucson, Phoenix, Reno, and Boise are on the frontlines of the anarch push. They control \u201cspecial agents\u201d of the highway patrol to stop and search trucks passing through Arizona, Nevada, and Idaho. They are probably a combination of dominated or other controlled mortals in the various police, and special ghouls squads trained to kill Kindred. This seems local to the individual Princes there, but I assume Petrodon coordinates some of this.<br /> <br /> We also know some of the Princes sent their own agents to spy on the Free States. David Geduld was one such agent on behalf of Prince Lodin. Geduld arrived in 1963 and loyally reported back until 1965 when he decided to defect after the Sabbat invasion in 1965. Other Princes likely have their own agents there as well (especially the aforementioned Tucson, Phoenix, Reno, and Boise). How much of their information, or identities, is provided to Petrodon is unknown. I\u2019m guessing very little although that might change if Petrodon switches to active plans of attack.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re also told of at least one agent among the named characters, Gloria Martinez. She was a street smart gang girl dominated by Petrodon who later found Salvador Garcia\u2019s haven, confronted him, and told him to either embrace her or kill her, and impressed by her gumption he embraced her. However, she remains a sleeper agent of Petrodon, likely under a lot of conditioning. Her embrace date is given as 1972 which indicates Petrodon was doing things way before his 1984 instructions. She is listed as merely the \u201cmost influential\u201d of \u201cseveral agents\u201d that Petrodon has planted in the Free States.<br /> <br /> We also know that Tara wants to be independent and rule San Diego on her own, and is considering to defect to the Camarilla. Tara\u2019s issues with the Free States are sufficient that this is actually a rumor among the anarchs themselves. I assume that Petrodon must be in touch with Tara in some capacity. Probably ready to confirm her status as Prince of San Diego when he launches his attack on the Free States.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of things in LABN, Petrodon\u2019s agents and plans seem like it would be an important thing, but it is very underdeveloped in the sourcebook. While it\u2019s always good to allow STs some freedom to customize their chronicles, I feel it would have been better to provide more material that STs could use and be inspired from to create their own plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-28T10:46:18-07:00","id":1549617,"title":"","content":"We can fill in some other details using other sources. Most of these were published well after the LABN sourcebook, and while these were not intended to be statements about the Camarilla\u2019s operations against the Free States, we can retcon a lot of this in.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu Gary Golden is primogen in the Bloodlines game, and it is plausible he provided information to Petrodon as part of the general Nosferatu information network, perhaps even recruited. Presumably despite being embraced in the Free States, he did not form a high opinion of it. That game also has a Nosferatu elder, Betram Tung, who\u2019s loyal to Golden, so he could be another Nosferatu willing to share information with Petrodon and other Camarilla loyal Nosferatu even if this is done more for clan reasons than preference for the Camarilla. Likewise, the Malkavian Alistar Grout is primogen in the same game and could have provided information to Petrodon. He also likely pre-dates the creation of the Free States. I am making an assumption here that becoming primogen after being long time residents in the Free States indicates some amount of cooperation prior to the Free States fall and thus proven &quot;loyalty&quot; to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Calvin Cleaver is from Children of the Night. He was a Vietnam War veteran and LA native embraced by a Gangrel in 1977 who subsequently made his way east, recruited with another half dozen Kindred, and then sent back to LA to keep an eye on the Anarch Free States in the mid/late eighties. That sounds a lot like he was recruited by one of Petrodon\u2019s archons. That would mirror in some ways the Wolfpack in CBN as they had one member who was an archon, and the rest were just his buddies. This groups seems to have been known to the local anarchs, but since they avoided trouble through diplomacy, it\u2019s likely the anarchs thought they were either just more anarchs or typical wandering Gangrel who didn\u2019t care about politics.<br /> <br /> Petrodon should have an Alastor, and it makes sense she would target Germaine as this target combines both her job to hunt anathema and Petrodon\u2019s remit against the anarchs. Since alastors also act as a kind of secret police in Camarilla domains, one of the archons stationed in San Francisco could be an alastor, and this actually works out well for Countess D\u2019adhemar if she\u2019s in that domain as well.<br /> <br /> The Archons and Templars sourcebook describe a type of archon called quaesitors who are (usually) Tremere concerned with all things magical. Since the anarchs do have their own blood magic in certain rituals and other unusual means, it would make sense for Petrodon to have one whose concern would be to research this and eventually work to eliminate this factor when the Camarilla attacks. Since I intend to use whatever lore exists on anarch blood magic in this campaign, this kind of agent makes a lot of sense for my chronicle. He should be collecting whatever information he can, by whatever means he can, about these strange blood magicians among the anarchs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-28T13:34:20-07:00","id":1549620,"title":"","content":"Seeing the Princes of Tucson, Phoenix. Reno and Boise mentioned persuaded me to do some research - so far as I can tell, only Tucson has a named Prince in any version of canon, with Lettow Kominsky of Clan Gangrel being depicted in the video game NIGHT ROAD (Though it\u2019s mentioned that he took charge after a former Prince of the city was slain by his fellow Ventrue, suggesting a possible plot hook - with Germain or other Anarch provocateurs raising rebellion in that city against the former Prince).<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the cities themselves, probable numbers for local vampires will be (Based on urban and metro population numbers circa AD q2020):-<br /> <br /> TUCSON (8 to 10)<br /> <br /> PHOENIX (16 to 48)<br /> <br /> RENO (3 to 5)<br /> <br /> BOISE (2 to 8)<br /> <br /> <br /> By the look of things these Princes are likely to be middleweights in the main, but fairly secure against internal rivals (Given these cities aren\u2019t likely to support a mass of potential rivals): the obvious exception is, of course, Phoenix - as a city on it\u2019s way to being a Big Deal, it may be sensible to sketch out the local Kindred and get a clear picture of the local Prince, because that one is only going to get more important, whether they\u2019re fit to wield that authority or not).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-28T14:05:38-07:00","id":1549621,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, you\u2019ve done a good job of sketching out the basic situation with Petrodon, so I\u2019ll only add a few notions (Though I\u2019ll keep thinking over the weekend):-<br /> <br /> - Petrodon (Embraced AD 1348) almost certainly experienced and survived the First Anarch Revolt, which would definitely influence his attitude to the Second.<br /> <br /> - His first known Childe (Julio Martinez) was embraced in AD 1437, to be employed as a spy: it\u2019s possible he was literally created to infiltrate the OG Anarch movement (Or at least it\u2019s predecessors).<br /> <br /> He was also captured by the Sabbat and \u2018turned\u2019, which may help explain Petrodon\u2019s cautious approach to the Anarchs (or perhaps his sudden shift): he\u2019s reacting to the sudden, nasty reality that a considerable part of his operations have been compromised (Though Petrodon seems to favour a hands-off approach which may mean his operations are sufficiently well-compartmentalised for quite a few to go on regardless).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Incidentally, I presume that Petrodon is of the 6th Generation and that his Childe Julio Martinez lowered his Generation via diablerie whilst with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> - Petrodon being a Spanish speaking Elder may help explain why he\u2019s mostly keeping clear of LA: quite a few of the local Anarchs may hear the accent of Old Spain and think of the late, unlamented Don Sebastian.<br /> <br /> - Incidentally, his full name is given as Count Alonso Cristo Petrodon of Seville: given his Sire was one Cristo, it\u2019s<br /> possible he was turned by a distant relation.<br /> <br /> - My impression is that Petrodon does favour a hand\u2019s-off approach (Working through agents and other proxies) partly because he likes to think of himself as a kind, forbearing sort of authority figure, but that when he moves he moves fast and Big (For example, toppling the New England Triad in AD 1990 after being absent from the region for a hundred years or more).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, he made his Big Move in New England by toppling Stanford Warwick, suggesting he might have created a fair number of grudges in his own Clan.<br /> <br /> <br /> - One last point: his treatment of Cock Robin (Whom he sired on a whim, deserted, then somehow secured the support of as a crucial precondition for his Big Move in New England and promoted within Camarilla circles until the latter was his logical successor as Nosferatu Justicar) strongly suggests that Petrodon has something of an \u2018artistic temperament\u2019 - at times moved by short term passions, but creative enough to spin whims into long term designs AND bring them in for a smooth landing,<br /> <br /> I suspect it\u2019s the mix of deliberate planning and improvisation that has allowed Petrodon to rise so high and put himself in a position to raise one of his prot\u00e9g\u00e9s to the rank of Brujah Justicar (A degree of influence I suspect to be unusual, even in an Elder of the Ivory Tower).<br /> <br /> <br /> My apologies for this being so untidy - I\u2019m typing in between scenes from the finale to this latest season of REACHER.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-28T14:20:35-07:00","id":1549622,"title":"","content":"P.S. It has occurred to me that since Alonzo Guillen is also a Spanish Nosferatu of aristocratic descent embraced by a Spanish Nosferatu who employs a noble title (and since Guillen is of the Ninth Generation, his Sire of the Eighth) it\u2019s quite plausible that they hail from the bloodline of Petrodon (Possibly even by way of his Childe Julio Martinez, before the latter lowered his generation by Diablerie).<br /> <br /> This would, if nothing else, help create a potentially interesting new web of connections in the LA area (Assuming Don Armando de Madrid showed up to support his grandsire, look for his Childe and either rescue or destroy his own Sire). <br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, if this were the case then this suggests that Petrodon may have been at the root of the bloodline\u2019s aristocratic tendencies (Since his sire is just plain \u2018Cristo\u2019, a name possibly adopted because that individual was one of the first Iberian vampires to adopt the Christian faith, whether within his own Clan or first amongst all the vampires of what would become Spain &amp; Portugal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-29T01:55:36-07:00","id":1549629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla?p=1549620#post1549620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Seeing the Princes of Tucson, Phoenix. Reno and Boise mentioned persuaded me to do some research.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reno and Boise are relatively unimportant cities by their numbers, but Boise is the state capital of Idaho and Reno is relatively close to Carson City which is the sate capital of Nevada. So control over the state police - aka the highway patrol - lies in those cities. Same goes with Phoenix, but as you stated Phoenix is much bigger city, and will eventually become a much larger city after 1994. Control here does allow some meaningful interdiction between the Free States and targets farther inland, but the Anarch Council isn't stupid either so it's mostly a draw with each side regretting what it can't do.<br /> <br /> Boise and Reno are perhaps somewhat safe by their distance from the Free States, but Phoenix becomes an important factor due to its high growth rate. It becomes both a target by the Free States, and a worrisome bastion of the Camarilla if left alone. I do have existing ideas of how to portray this. It also helps that while Phoenix is a relatively new city, especially in terms of size, that Tucson is quite old for a city in the southwestern US. Still not large in absolute terms, but it was bigger than Phoenix until the 1920s.<br /> <br /> Except for some far-sighted Kindred, the anarchs of Los Angeles don't see this. Their previous success and size kind of make them arrogant in regards to Phoenix. They're in LA after all, and what the hell is in Phoenix (or Arizona in general)?<br /> <br /> If only Tombstone had continued to grow!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jGJc3Vv_-Qw\" data-code=\"jGJc3Vv_-Qw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jGJc3Vv_-Qw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T15:28:32-07:00","id":1549688,"title":"","content":"Much to my relief, the Tucson Prison Complex opened in AD 1982, which means my pet theory about the Prince of Tucson having a potentially useful recruiting ground for ghouls (or \u2018wine press\u2019 for vampires with a knack for the working the system and/or a taste for \u2018Rough Trade\u2019) can be advanced in the context of a 1990s start date.<br /> <br /> Whether this is or is not the case, even a cursory reading of Tucson\u2019s history makes it clear this is a settlement with \u201cCity of the Wild West Vampires\u201d written all over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T16:53:27-07:00","id":1549689,"title":"","content":"How many more Dominated agents should Petrodon and the Camarilla have in LA?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not clear to me whether Gloria Martinez\u2019s status is due to Conditioning, or if it should be from an elder power of Dominate or perhaps a combination Discipline. I remember seeing similar effects elsewhere. I could swear there was some scenario set in Chicago that had said if a certain anarch observed a Masquerade breach, he would eventually sneak away to make a telephone call from a payphone and inform someone (I can\u2019t find this now in my sourcebooks, so I wonder if I just made that up.) There\u2019s nothing in the Conditioning power that says it cannot affect Kindred, but conditioning seems to obliterate their personality, and this doesn\u2019t seem to be the case if these Telefon-like hypnotized sleeper agents. Still, it doesn\u2019t rule out the idea that you can condition someone so that while their personality is mostly intact, that one or a few \u201cconditioned\u201d responses are implanted so the Kindred either forgets they did them (like calling someone and providing them information) or subconsciously influences certain decisions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XQ9IZL5VC3M\" data-code=\"XQ9IZL5VC3M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XQ9IZL5VC3M/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Or maybe just the Naked Gun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cq2CfdYVgwg\" data-code=\"cq2CfdYVgwg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/cq2CfdYVgwg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I\u2019m personally fine with such an interpretation of Conditioning (within limits), but I don\u2019t know what other players would think about it.<br /> <br /> Whatever it is, it is enough that she was not only dominated thoroughly as a mortal, but that it survived the embrace. (Again, whether something like this really works with Conditioning as written is debatable.) Does this status need to be renewed every once in a while? If it is Conditioning, the Kindred does not need to make eye contact or be present, just heard. So merely a phone call can do it, and it only needs to be done every four months or so in Gloria\u2019s case.<br /> <br /> With Gloria the initial conditioning was easy because as a mortal, her disappearance for a week would not be suspicious as it\u2019d be unnoticed by vampires. However, I can\u2019t imagine there are many conditioned mortals who subsequently became vampires. Gloria may be unique in this case. So if there are other conditioned deep agent Kindred in the Free States, they would need to be conditioned after they became vampires.<br /> <br /> It is possible that non-native vampires could have been conditioned, and then subsequently sent to the Free States. However, I don\u2019t think there are very many of them. While not mentioned in LABN, the Anarch Cookbook has an anarch ritual where it is possible to tell if a Kindred is under the influence of dominate. I will be using that in my own LABN chronicle, and this is used to check out many new Kindred arriving just to make sure they aren\u2019t unsuspecting secret agents. I\u2019m sure some may have been successfully inserted at some point, but others were found out. It\u2019d be an unreliable method.<br /> <br /> A safer would be a way to conditioning a vampire already in the Free States, as these would be unlikely to be checked or checked again. But a vampire missing for a long enough time to be conditioned could be noticed by their coterie. It would also require the Camarilla to send an agent into the Free States first and risk being discovered. Or possibly wait for certain Kindred to leave (perhaps going to one of the outer free states or even a domain like San Francisco, and attempt to get them then). This method has its own risks of detection.<br /> <br /> While Petrodon and his archons are the obvious origins of dominated Kindred like this, there are plenty of other people who would want their own agents inside the Free States like Countess D'adhemar, nearby Princes, and even internal enemies like Mohammed al-Muthlin and Tara.<br /> <br /> I am probably overthinking things like usual, but I prefer to think things through in order to understand how things can be done in practice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T17:04:26-07:00","id":1549691,"title":"","content":"What will happen to Gloria Martinez when the Camarilla decides to attack? Is she just someone used to obtain information, or is the intention to use her afterwards? That she is called a \u201cfifth column\u201d implies she may actually do some fighting when the time comes. After all, we know from Chicago By Night that Lodin used Hinds against his old socialist allies, and dominated Uriah so that he betrayed Maldavis.<br /> <br /> One thing I am considering is whether the \u201cgang\u201d Gloria has built and leading may be something Petrodon hopes to use. Are the seven vampires around Whittier that Gloria leads Kindred who may fight for the Camarilla if the circumstances are right?<br /> <br /> She would need to recruit vampires native to LA. Any vampire who arrived from outside would probably already be anarchs and unlikely to defect. But not every vampire embraced in LA would naturally be on the side of the anarchs if the domain was not already ruled by the anarchs. There are enough negatives to the Free States that some vampires may prefer the stability of the Camarilla, or convinced to go along if they are provided enough incentive.<br /> <br /> Of course, they\u2019d need to be Kindred who would not normally suffer under a typical domain. So no Caitiff. Any Brujah would need to carefully considered. However, Kindred of other clans would be much less likely to suffer.<br /> <br /> We are told that the vampires in Whittier are \u201cmore upscale\u201d and want to be \u201cleft alone\u201d. This is precisely what we might expect from a gang not happy with how the Free States are run, and are possibly being groomed to prefer the Camarilla when the attack finally happens. It certainly doesn't sound like the kind of &quot;gang&quot; that a &quot;smart gang girl&quot; from an impoverished barrio would normally gather around her. Especially since the description mentioned that Salvador mentored her to develop her Disciplines so she could &quot;protect and defend her community rather than escape from it.&quot; Yet it seems she did just that. It's at times like these I don't know whether the author intended this to be subtle clues for the reader to figure out, or if he was just lazy and careless about putting things together.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Kindred of this gang are consciously choosing the Camarilla. Just that they'd be Kindred who outsiders could judge as candidates to defect when the circumstances are right. I have to give some thought as to the kinds of character concepts and personalities that seem on the surface to be typical anarchs, but if revealed to be betrayers, it would not be inconceivable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T23:33:36-07:00","id":1550832,"title":"","content":"More archaeology from the Anarch Cookbook. In its section on media it states that the Camarilla still strong in Hollywood, and that it is a hot battlefground between the anarchs and Camarilla. The Ventrue still retain powerful control over financing in Hollywood while the Brujah are strong on the creative end and Hollywood unions. <br /> <br /> There's even an example mechanics section that has Petrodon rolling his Manipulation + Influence (difficulty 8) to prevent a film release that is a possible threat to the Masquerade. While we're not given a dice pool, we are told Petrodon got five successes which implies a very big dice pool and thus high Influence in Hollywood. While this is obviously for game running purposes and not necessarily canon stats, I do take it to mean that Petrodon does have considerable influence even if he uses it to protect harm against the Masquerade or prevent scandalous references to known Camarilla princes and other officials.<br /> <br /> What exactly does that mean? It's highly unlikely the Ventrue or Petrodon visit Hollywood so their Influence must be done remotely and long distance. Nevertheless their control over financing, production, and distribution has to be substantial.<br /> <br /> If face to face meetings are necessary, does it happen in San Francisco? Do they retain a large number of ghouls, allies, dominated or bribed mortals in Hollywood itself? Where are the Camarilla vampires located who retain this influence? Given this importance are they archons? Refugees who once lived in Los Angeles? Deep cover agents? Do they ever risk coming to Los Angeles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T12:44:22-07:00","id":1550851,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Petrodon makes moves in (and against) Hollywood via LA vampires who aren\u2019t Camarilla but are open to doing business with all parties? (Going by the status quo in BLOODLINES the first, it\u2019s possible to imagine Isaac Abrams discretely arranging some quid pro quo with the Camarilla, possibly through Sebastian LaCroix).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also very plausible that Petrodon worked through mortal agents discretely backed up by Kindred support - all the better to make things look beneath interest for the Anarchs and emphasise the Camarilla preference for discretion over Direct Action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T20:32:40-07:00","id":1550931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla?p=1550851#post1550851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Petrodon makes moves in (and against) Hollywood via LA vampires who aren\u2019t Camarilla but are open to doing business with all parties? (Going by the status quo in BLOODLINES the first, it\u2019s possible to imagine Isaac Abrams discretely arranging some quid pro quo with the Camarilla, possibly through Sebastian LaCroix).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sure there are plenty of vampires in LA willing to work with Petrodon or other Camarilla vampires in general. The problem is from a risk/reward perspective. If ever discovered, those vampires are likely to be destroyed as traitors. So what rewards would be worth that risk?<br /> <br /> Some risk could be transferred from potential collaborators by making them deal with agents in LA not known to be Camarilla. Then Isaac Abrams (or whoever) would work together without considering the risk because from his perspective there is none. Even if Isaac later became suspicion and the agents were later discovered, Isaac could still correctly say they didn't know and still possibly survive. Of course, then all the risk is put on those agents. They'd really need to be committed and would likely need to be deep cover agents whose &quot;passions&quot; are things like keeping the Masquerade or other innocent activities that don't arouse suspicions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla?p=1550851#post1550851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s also very plausible that Petrodon worked through mortal agents discretely backed up by Kindred support - all the better to make things look beneath interest for the Anarchs and emphasise the Camarilla preference for discretion over Direct Action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortal agents are the way to go with influence, but how are they recruited? Ghouls could easily defect. Supernatural control would need to be reinforced every so often. There's a lot of chance such efforts would be overridden by local vampires whose ease of access makes it easier for them to cultivate influence and inadvertently steal agents away.<br /> <br /> Media industry people do often travel away from SoCal so there are other opportunities to cultivate influence for Petrodon and other members of the Camarilla. It's just harder. Out of area resorts, film festivals, location shooting or alternative lower cost productions (&quot;Hollywood North&quot; in Canada and such), sporting events, and business travel would be ways for Petrodon and others to make regular contact with certain people and maintain influence. But there's always a risk they lose out once their marks get back to LA.<br /> <br /> I know film finance often comes from money not &quot;native&quot; to LA, and presumably most Camarilla influence stems from that. However, you probably still need local people in key sectors.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T09:48:18-07:00","id":1550959,"title":"","content":"Your latter point rather dismisses the possibility of old-fashioned indoctrination (You don\u2019t need creepy supernatural powers to shape and maintain loyalty, just the right carrot and the stick - or more likely money, time and special attention) and the sort of worldly incentives available to a member of the Inner Council (Money again, power, access to the most interesting places and people etc).<br /> <br /> Whilst Awesome Vampire Powers are a key element of VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE, I suspect they\u2019re only one tool in the repertoire of the Elder Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T11:41:03-07:00","id":1550968,"title":"","content":"The Disciplines make for a great ace up your sleeve, but should be used as a last resort deal if other methods of persuasion fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T17:00:55-07:00","id":1550977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla?p=1550959#post1550959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your latter point rather dismisses the possibility of old-fashioned indoctrination (You don\u2019t need creepy supernatural powers to shape and maintain loyalty, just the right carrot and the stick - or more likely money, time and special attention) and the sort of worldly incentives available to a member of the Inner Council (Money again, power, access to the most interesting places and people etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>While the lack of distance might not dampen more mundane means of influence in other non-local industries, I think it might apply a lot less in Hollywood and the high end of the entertainment industry. People there are already fabulously rich, have high status. have access to sexual targets, hobnob with other rich and powerful people, have lots of esteem/validation, be in extremely glamorous surroundings, and so on. Almost anything someone outside of LA could bring them, they already have access to in LA. Most of the time such local things will probably be preferred over non-local. In that kind of industry, only parts of New York (particularly Broadway, but also some TV, fine arts, music, and other legacy media) have equal or more prestige.<br /> <br /> (It's interesting to think maybe Petrodon has a Toreador archon whose main purpose is to cultivate that NYC arts &amp; entertainment influence for use against the LA anarchs. Just hope she isn't eaten by the Sabbat while doing it).<br /> <br /> It's not that such people still cannot be tempted, but more than nine times out of ten, if they have someone local offering it versus someone non-local, there just doing to go local. Relationships need to be maintained for that kind of thing, and proximity makes it easier to develop and maintain relationships.<br /> <br /> LABN makes it seem that all anarchs are simply brutish gangbangers, but that is also one of the flaws of that sourcebook. There are going to be a certain number of anarchs who are part of the Hollywood movie and TV industry, and they are just going to be better at developing most relationships with industry bigshots than someone not local.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that LA should have a significant number of vampires with the Fame attribute. Lots of concepts of vampires actresses, musicians, other artists, idols, and celebrities out there. Their personal connections (likely made when they were still mortal) are going to count for a lot.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that means it is impossible for Petrodon and other Camarilla members to have influence there. They should to a degree, and I think such influence struggles will make for a more compelling game experience for the PCs. However, I do think Petrodon and company are under a handicap here. I think it's a smart idea to step back and consider how they can cultivate what resources they can and how to leverage it best. If they are too obvious or direct, they risk losing their agents of influence. I default to a position that Petrodon has a relative weak hand in this compared to the anarchs, but that he manages to play it well and wins more often than he should. The difficulty for me is working out how he does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T19:37:02-07:00","id":1551035,"title":"","content":"As a spin off to something <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council/page4#post1550932\">discussed in a post on the Anarch Council thread</a>, i want to consider the idea of a Warwick's Web type intelligence network of the Nosferatu on the Pacific Coast. Possibly based in Seattle because if the center of the web is in Seattle, it would explain why Petrodon decided to base his operations there.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is completely non-canon, but it's also the case that the Nosferatu methuselah Trajan must have other webs around the world. LABN does mention that the Triad fighting over New England have agents in the area. Dark Selina's is supposedly Christopher Houghton himself (somehow - how these methuselahs actually manipulate or control things is never defined), but the other two only have agents of much less power. In Trajan's case, it would make sense it would be someone working for the web.<br /> <br /> The Webs seem to have a simple structure. There is someone at the center, whose title/position is not given. I imagine it's something like webmaster or spider. Dark Colony just says that the headquarters of the Web is the &quot;Lair&quot;. Maybe I'll just use that. If someone has an idea for a cooler name for this position, I'm interested in hearing it. It's not clear if these webmasters report directly to Trajan (or when Trajan was in torpor to his second in command), but I would guess so. Then we have &quot;strand masters&quot; who are in charge of a region. In New England, these were Home Strand, Vermont Strand, Connecticut Strand, and Maine Strand. Nosferatu responsible for an individual city or county were &quot;district overseers&quot;. Then there were deep infiltration agents called &quot;veins&quot;. Any other Nosferatu just collecting information are simply termed &quot;operatives&quot;. Warwick's web comprised around a dozen Nosferatu so each Strand on the average only had three. So once we assume one Strand Master and an additional District Overseer for each Strand, there's not much room left over for veins and operatives. I assume some Strands have more and others less. It is possible that Veins are not based on individual Strands and move around at the behest of their Strandmaster or Lair.<br /> <br /> If we use this same structure for the Pacific Coast, we have a Lair in Seattle and Strand Masters that probably cover Washington, Oregon, North/Central California, and possibly elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I won't have an LA Strandmaster because I do want the Los Angeles Nosferatu to mostly be loyal to the anarchs, but I will make one be a District Overseer who reports to the Strand Master in San Francisco. There might also be one Vein who is under deep cover in Los Angeles with an alternate identity and high enough Obufscate not to be identified as a Nosferatu spy.<br /> <br /> Not all Nosferatu are part of the Web. Members have a special commitment to Trajan's Web. Most local Nosferatu just do their own thing. However, members of Trajan's Web do have access to a lot of juicy gossip from outside the local warren. Just as Petrodon uses it to get some insight into what is going on in Los Angeles, Nosferatu anarchs occasionally benefit from this too. Trajan himself doesn't really care about sect disputes and local politics. He has the typical elder Nosferatu concerns about Nictuku and such, and his own feuds with other methuselahs operating at his level. Petrodon is just able to utilize this Web already in place because he is a powerful and influential Nosferatu now local to Seattle. However, he does not control it, and whatever information he &quot;takes&quot; from it, he also &quot;gives&quot; an equivalent back because that is simply clan culture. Still this is an important advantage he has.<br /> <br /> It's likely one of the PCs will be a Nosferatu so this is something that should be discovered early on, and it'll be interesting to see how the PC reacts. Of course, the Nosferatu member on the Anarch Council also knows this exists and has figured out who the LA District Overseer is. But I intend for the identity of this Nosferatu is unknown (outside to the members of the Anarch Council) and is one of the mysteries that PCs may or may not figure out on their own.<br /> <br /> However, the main reason I'm including this is that I have always loved Warwick's Web in Dark Colony. The evocative titles for its agents are great. Dark Colony is an extremely flawed sourcebook, but it has a few great things, and this is one. I was disappointed when I did not see this concept utilized again in future sourcebooks and the revised Nosferatu clanbook. Trajan's Web should be a huge setting element IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T13:55:09-07:00","id":1551050,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Dark Selina\u2019s method of influencing - I refuse to believe she can actually control the Evil Peter Pan of LA - Christopher was to put Jeremy MacNeil in his vicinity? (Since Dark Selina seems to be fairly anti-Camarilla, it\u2019s<br /> possible that she gambled on the Eternal Rebel and his handsome self swaying Christopher to the point of making a serious mess of the structure his descendants had built up in Southern California).<br /> <br /> Dark Selina is unquestionably a Brujah, after all, even if this seems to be all that is verifiably known about her (Also that she was already old in the very early 1700s), so it\u2019s not impossible that she might have sufficiently connections throughout the Clan to have a sense of who MacNeil is and where he might be headed.<br /> <br /> This does rather beg the question of how she knows about Christopher, but given her Childe (Roman Pendragon) has strong ties to New England, it\u2019s far from impossible that Christopher has been on her radar since the latter was in Boston with his Sire - could he have headed for California specifically after his immortal humiliation because Dark Selina pointed him in that direction? (I\u2019m assuming that her plan, at this point, was nothing more detailed than \u201cIf this man-child is the first vampire in any area, at some future point I can wreck anything built in that area with a strong sneeze\u201d).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, regarding LA Nosferatu being relatively loyal to the Anarch Free State, I wonder if this could be grounded in historic persecution by the local Toreador under Don Sebastian as steered by Christopher? (It\u2019s completely straightforward to imagine the latter as a \u201cYuck! I hate it, get rid of it!\u201d sort of Toreador - and the fact that the first Nosferatu in the LA area wasn\u2019t exactly a beacon of charm may well have persuaded Don Sebastian that Clan was only slightly less feral than the Gangrel).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T13:44:15-07:00","id":1551080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla?p=1551050#post1551050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, regarding LA Nosferatu being relatively loyal to the Anarch Free State, I wonder if this could be grounded in historic persecution by the local Toreador under Don Sebastian as steered by Christopher?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously there's no canonical statement about that as the LABN sourcebook only has one Nosferatu character in it who dwells by himself in the San Gabriel hills. The entire clan is pretty much ignored just like the Gangrel (who don't even get one NPC description!).<br /> <br /> I made that decision for several reasons. 1) Since one of the PCs will be Nosferatu, I don't want a situation where the coterie is confronted with an entire clan being disloyal to the Free States. It would create a bad dynamic and put that PC into a real bind. 2) I assume just like any clan, Nosferatu anarchs in other cities will travel to the Free States and thus be prominent members of their clan. In turn these Nosferatu anarchs will embrace new fledglings and be raised to be anarchs. So there's obviously going to be anarch Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Does that mean all Nosferatu are strictly loyal to the Free States? Of course not. You will have several groups. One are loyal anarchs. Another is a group that just accepts the domain is anarch and adjust. What does it matter to them who is in charge? It won't change how Nosferatu treat each other. A third group are Nosferatu who are not happy about the anarchs being in control, but aren't going to do anything about it. Regardless of their preference, it's the way things are. Best for all Nosferatu to get along. Probably only a small group are both upset that the anarchs are in control and willing to do something about it. In this case, help the Camarilla secretly and don't mention it to the others. So regardless of the actual demographic breakdown of the Nosferatu clan, it'll seem like they're loyal overall.<br /> <br /> If the PCs want to dig deeper and uncover the actual motivations and loyalties of individual Nosferatu, they need to figure that out on her own.<br /> <br /> Now, it's not a bad idea to say that Don Sebastian and the LA Toreador were real asses to the Nosferatu when they were in power, and as a result the clan didn't mind the anarchs wiping them out. That's a good angle to use. It's not unusual for those clans to not get along. It doesn't even need to be objectively true. Just what's told to new arrivals or embraces to explain why there may be some pre-1944 Nosferatu around. Or what attracted some Nosferatu to support the anarchs afterwards or attract more Nosferatu who harbor their own anti-Toreador prejudices.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T14:00:22-07:00","id":1551083,"title":"","content":"I admit to reading the almost complete absence of Nosferatu of note from LA BY NIGHT from a Watsonian perspective - while it\u2019s perfectly possible the Clan\u2019s absence is based on the writer having no ideas for them, I prefer to infer that this suggests the Clan to be very thin on the ground in that area (Quite possibly because the only elder of note in the region seems more interested in wandering than socialising) and/or that most of those present will be relatively puny specimens.<br /> <br /> With this is mind the traditional hostility between Toreador &amp; Nosferatu made as logical a reason for this stage of affairs as any other, especially given that the former Prince of the Ckty had a long record of running LA as a \u2018Sundown Town\u2019* for Kindred he didn\u2019t much like (and the fairly aggressive tendencies of the the Free State Anarchs would probably not appeal very much to a Clan traditionally depicted as fond of the quiet life).<br /> <br /> It must be said, I really like your notion that most local Nosferatu are young and hungry Anarchs deliberately working to get out from under their elders (Although the traditional close-knit nature of the Clan suggests that these would be somewhat unusual and in a much more vulnerable position than most of their bloodline - possibly explaining their relatively unimpressive standing).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Or in this case \u2018Sunrise Town\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T23:36:49-07:00","id":1551288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla?p=1551083#post1551083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit to reading the almost complete absence of Nosferatu of note from LA BY NIGHT from a Watsonian perspective</div> </div> </div> </div>If that produces good results for you at the game table, more power to you. However, I don't think that is intentional. There's not even a single Gangrel character mentioned in the NPC section. No page for Gangrel at all. Yet at various points in the LABN sourcebook, they make reference to Gangrels. The reason there are no Gangrel mentioned and only one Nosferatu mentioned in the entire NPC section isn't because they don't exist in the setting. It's because the sourcebook writer didn't think there were any &quot;important&quot; such characters in the local area (for whatever definition of &quot;important&quot;), or at least didn't have the page count for them. (However, he was very interested in the Vignes family drama which Alonzo is part of which is why this irrelevant subplot takes up so many pages in LABN.)<br /> <br /> Given LA urban lore and legends like various secret (but real) underground tunnels, the lizard people's catacombs discovered by George Warren Shufelt, and the millions of rats living in LA's palm trees, LA is a great place for Nosferatu. I'll be taking advantage of all of that for the local LA Nosferatu in my chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T13:06:39-07:00","id":1551347,"title":"","content":"Fair enough - I\u2019ll only add that it\u2019s sometimes interesting to shake up expectations and keep readers (or, one supposes, players) on their toes by introducing a setting apparently built for a certain group, showing the place nonetheless mysteriously bereft of said group and allowing the audience\u2019s own suspicions to enliven their experience as we all explore WHY prime real estate might be found currently-unoccupied (After all, it\u2019s not as if the World of Darkness has only one faction that enjoys underground living and the Nosferatu can\u2019t have won ALL their dice rolls over the centuries).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T00:51:50-07:00","id":1551363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla?p=1551347#post1551347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">showing the place nonetheless mysteriously bereft of said group and allowing the audience\u2019s own suspicions to enliven their experience as we all explore WHY prime real estate might be found currently-unoccupied</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not bad for a general chronicle that otherwise doesn't have anything &quot;special&quot; about it. We all need certain chronicle mysteries, tentpoles, or plot hooks. However, as the showcase of the anarch experience, I already have a huge distinguishing feature for LA. If I introduce yet another thing, which is completely independent of its anarch nature, I think it'll detract rather than add to what should be the main attraction of the setting.<br /> <br /> The total absence of the Nosferatu in a chronicle could be done in any chronicle. It is an interesting hook on its own. But it's something that could equally apply to a Camarilla or Sabbat chronicle. I'd rather concentrate on things that apply to a chronicle set in the Free States which would not apply in a typical Camarilla chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T00:11:33-07:00","id":1551408,"title":"","content":"There's one obvious group of Camarilla in Los Angeles I haven't mentioned yet; the Brujah Idealists. These are the four Brujah who arrived in the Free States to study it. Some are sympathetic to the anarchs and others hostile, but all are ostensibly loyal to the Camarilla. The coterie is an interesting concept that I haven't quite figure out how to use in a chronicle. As fairly passive observers, they actually lack obvious hooks. Yet they seem like they should be something that is interesting for PCs to encounter and interact with.<br /> <br /> I've long felt that the original Brujah Clanbook's division of &quot;iconoclasts&quot;, &quot;individualists&quot;, and &quot;idealists&quot; is something more like how an anthropologist would categorize things than categories a group would divide themselves in. So I'll use this group as a way to &quot;introduce&quot; these concepts, since they are essentially anthropologists and political scientists. It's one thing I can do with them at least.<br /> <br /> Another thing is to make sure they are not passive scholars. Most Kindred in the Free States know about them, and treat them in the same way many countries treat Western media - a way to get out their message and propagandize. Eventually what the &quot;Brujah Idealists&quot; (I really need a better name for them) study is going to be reported back to many of the salons of the Camarilla. I need to have them attend Rants, interview the various barons, ask regular anarchs to complete questionnaires and such like. <br /> <br /> Everyone knows they are essentially Camarilla loyalists, but no one does anything against them because it'd be counter productive. If you are a Third World terrorist, you don't kidnap or kill Western journalists. You try to use them to your advantage to get out the story you want to tell. For many Brujah anarchs, they seem them as loyal clanmates. They might be wrong, but they are still trustworthy and worthy of respect. The non-Brujah anarchs might resent that, but there are just too many Brujah anarchs that you can't ignore their feelings on this matter.<br /> <br /> Everyone knows some (maybe everything) of what they learn is going to go to Petrodon, but so what? They know Petrodon already has agents and spies in the Free States. He's going to learn what the Brujah Idealists learn anyway. They aren't going to uncover any secrets that Petrodon won't learn on his own. So treat them with kindness and earn goodwill. Just don't tell them any actual important secrets.<br /> <br /> I wonder if it might be a good idea to split up the four different Idealists into different anarch groups/gangs/baronies. Each one studies a different group and then shares his learnings with the others and then discuss what he's learned with the group.<ul><li>Sir Ralph Hamilton - as the conservative most pro-Camarilla Brujah, he'd be good to approach the least radical anarchs (which in my chronicle would be Kindred like Fortier and Geduld)</li> <li>Professor Gregory Habersohn - as a non-judgmental academic, he'd be good to approach those anarchs least willing to trust the group as he could best win them over eventually</li> <li>Dr. Shiraiwa Takuya - as a Stalinist Communist, he'd be a good choice for the most radical, revolutionary anarchs.</li> <li>Countess Andrea Visconti - as a flamboyant gallant, she'd be good at charming many of the youngest anarchs without clear politics</li> </ul>One or more members will almost always be at every Rant. And instead of them being together, each will be split up, hanging out with one of &quot;their&quot; anarch groups. Whenever the PCs visit one of the barons or other important factions, they might encounter one of the Idealists already there. They may or may not be witnesses to a conversation with the PCs, but they will be ubiquitous and often seen.<br /> <br /> Finally, since they all dwell together in the &quot;Laurel Canyon House&quot;, it'd be good to make that an actual landmark in the Free States. Have &quot;open nights&quot; when any Kindred is welcome to arrive and share their story. Many anarchs might very well go there simply to vent and complain, happy that someone - anyone - is willing to hear their side of the story. Or even important individuals go to relate the propaganda they want to get out there, just like how many dictators will use the foreign press. That way it might be something one or more of the PCs decide to do themselves, or perhaps try to exploit that. They may even host certain events or salons or parties there because informal gatherings is a great way to cultivate contacts and informants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T08:55:07-07:00","id":1551540,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t have anything to add other than \u201cSir Ralph Hamilton ABSOLUTELY pronounces his name \u2018Rafe\u2019 rather than \u2018Ral-fuh\u2019 for that extra posh element.<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m now wondering just how many \u2018Lady Hamilton\u2019 jokes he\u2019s had to endure since the Napoleonic Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T16:08:31-07:00","id":1551547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla?p=1551540#post1551540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t have anything to add other than \u201cSir Ralph Hamilton ABSOLUTELY pronounces his name \u2018Rafe\u2019 rather than \u2018Ral-fuh\u2019 for that extra posh element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Good call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T13:04:59-08:00","id":1557994,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, it\u2019s been a while but I was just doing some casual research into the Dramatis Personae of BLOODLINES 2 and it suddenly struck me that Seattle having something of an Anarch problem, despite being the residence of a no-kidding Justicar of the Camarilla (Even a relatively lenient one like Petrodon) makes a lot more sense if the game canon that Seattle\u2019s Prince is seriously underage by vampire standards also applies to your own continuity.<br /> <br /> In fact Seattle having a relatively weak (or at least very young) Prince, whether that\u2019s Lou Graham or JJ Campbell) would be a logical draw for both Petrodon and the Anarchs - one looking to prop them up, one hoping to pull them down and each able to operate more freely in the absence of a heavyweight Prince.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still learning about the dramatis personae in the game and will take the liberty of posting my thoughts on your threats afterwards, if I may (Since while your payers may never head so far north, events in Seattle are obviously going to have a serious effect on Petrodon\u2019s plans and his freedom to implement them in the wider West Coast).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-01T22:35:39-08:00","id":1558059,"title":"","content":"I think I briefly mentioned this before on this forum, but I actually ran a chronicle in Seattle (I used to live there) in the past. So while I have not detailed Seattle for my Anarch chronicle set in LA, I am using the memory of that to inform me what is happening there. I have not played Bloodlines 2 or read up on it on any wiki, but like most things I have no problem stealing from it anything I find useful, but it won't be canon in my chronicle. At some point, I may actually look it up on the White Wolf Wiki.<br /> <br /> In regards to the Prince of Seattle, I established a Malkavian as Prince in Seattle whose derangement made him fairly effective at times, but otherwise not opposed to the presence of Petrodon. He was fairly young, like Lodin. There was just enough leeway that there was an anarch presence in the Pacific Northwest despite some effective &quot;cleaning&quot; from the princes of Portland and Seattlle plus Petrodon's archons.<br /> <br /> Feel free to post your thoughts or expound of any specific NPCs. I ended up using a lot on the thread for San Francisco. Who knows, they may see some game play. Since I intend for the Vampire Club in San Francisco to be fairly important in the chronicle, I can always use visiting NPCs there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T09:40:59-08:00","id":1558074,"title":"","content":"Then I shall certainly do more research and do more thinking.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, what made you fix on a Malkavian for Seattle\u2019s Prince?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T09:41:55-08:00","id":1558075,"title":"","content":"Wait a minute, it just struck me that the Pacific Northwest has a fairly strong New England connection: was this Prince an escapee from the Camelot-mad Malkavians of Boston?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}